{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved the best accuracy (0.6315) at low cost (7.27 GPU hrs), outperforming config_003 (pca_n2000, same other settings) by ~1.3% while being 5x cheaper. This establishes scvi_n200 as the preferred RNA encoder. Uncertainty: we have only tested concat fusion with avgpool aggregation; it is unclear whether weighted fusion can further improve on 0.6315. This experiment (config_016) makes the minimal single-variable change from the best config—switching fusion from concat to weighted while keeping scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile, multimodal—directly testing whether weighted fusion yields a gain. It is the best use of experiment 3 because it exploits the strongest evidence (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool) at minimal additional cost (~7-8 GPU hrs, similar to config_002), reducing uncertainty about the fusion choice before committing budget to more expensive architectural changes (e.g., transformer aggregation or ViT image encoder). If weighted fusion helps, we can then layer in transformer aggregation; if not, we rule out that direction cheaply and pivot to exploring aggregation or image encoder upgrades in the remaining 6 experiments."
}

